    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4f47e976_c6ea2922",
        "filename": "common/thermal.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 156,
      "author": {
        "id": 1384810
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-10T10:27:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We have implemented and used “CONFIG_FAIL_SAFE_OFFSET” for the purpose to increment the base temp value for future use/calculations. We defined CONFIG_DPTF_FAIL_SAFE_OFFSET with initial value as 0 under /board/hatch/board.h \n\nAs per above comment/suggestion, we have below observations, \n(1) if we use “IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_DPTF_FAIL_SAFE_OFFSET)”, it throws an error as below because “IS_ENABLED()” API is expecting the macro to be defined without any value. \nError:  include/common.h:383:5: error: call to \u0027IS_ENABLED_BAD_ARGS\u0027 declared with attribute\nerror: CONFIG_DPTF_FAIL_SAFE_OFFSET must be \u003cblank\u003e, or not defined.\n(2) if we declare the “CONFIG_DPTF_FAIL_SAFE_OFFSET” without any value, then we can’t use it in “cur_temp +\u003d CONFIG_DPTF_FAIL_SAFE_OFFSET;” as per line number 64. \n\nSo, I would suggest to use this current guard for easy usage and better code readability.",
      "parentUuid": "e4d7c5c9_2954ce32",
